.TH BATTERY-REVAMPED 1 "2026-11-20" "battery-revamped" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
battery\-revamped \- battery charge, state and health in the tmux status bar
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B battery\-revamped
.RI [ options ]
.I command
.RI [ name ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B battery\-revamped
shows the charge of the laptop battery in the tmux status line, with its state, the remaining
time, the charger watts, the cycle count, the health, the drain rate, an estimate, a sparkline of
the recent readings and an alert icon. macOS is read from pmset, system_profiler and ioreg. Linux is read from
/sys/class/power_supply, with acpi as the fallback.
.PP
The entry point
.B battery\-revamped.tmux
runs
.B apply
once when tmux loads the plugin, which binds the popup key in one tmux call and replaces the placeholders in status\-left and status\-right: #{battery_percentage}, #{battery_icon}, #{battery_icon_charge}, #{battery_icon_status}, #{battery_color_fg}, #{battery_color_bg}, #{battery_color_charge_fg}, #{battery_color_charge_bg}, #{battery_color_status_fg}, #{battery_color_status_bg}, #{battery_graph}, #{battery_remain}, #{battery_charging_watts}, #{battery_cycles}, #{battery_health}, #{battery_drain_rate}, #{battery_estimate}, #{battery_sparkline}, #{battery_power_source}, #{battery_alert_icon}.
.PP
A status call prints the stored reading at once. When the reading is older than the interval it starts one in the background, so the status line never waits. With the options render mode a background process fills one tmux option per placeholder on every tick. Run with no command on a terminal, the tool offers a menu.
.PP
The drain rate compares the charge with a reading at least five minutes old, and the estimate divides the charge left by that rate. A value the host has no source for is empty.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B apply
Bind the key and fill the status placeholders.
.TP
.B list
Print every command apply would send.
.TP
.B status name
Print one placeholder.
.TP
.B refresh
Read the battery now.
.TP
.B card
Print every figure as a table.
.TP
.B popup
Open the battery card in a tmux popup.
.TP
.B popup\-card
Print the card and wait for a key.
.TP
.B daemon
Publish the placeholders on every tick.
.TP
.B doctor
Check this machine.
.TP
.B version
Print the version.
.TP
.B help
Print the help page.
.SH OPTIONS
Every setting is also a long option. The command line wins over the environment, the environment over the tmux option, and the tmux option over the default. A tmux option set to nothing counts as not set; a value given as nothing on the command line or in the environment is used as given. An icon, label or text set to off prints nothing.
.TP
.B \-\-json
With list, print the plan as one JSON object.
.TP
.B \-\-theme name
The look: kodougu, catppuccin\-mocha, catppuccin\-latte, dracula, nord, gruvbox, tokyo\-night, mono.
.TP
.B \-\-popup\-key value
Key of the card popup, or off. The default is M\-b.
.TP
.B \-\-popup\-width value
Width of the popup. The default is 44.
.TP
.B \-\-popup\-height value
Height of the popup. The default is 16.
.TP
.B \-\-interval value
Seconds a reading stays fresh, or minute. The default is 15.
.TP
.B \-\-detail\-interval value
Seconds the remaining time, watts, cycles and health stay fresh. The default is 60.
.TP
.B \-\-render value
Jobs or options. The default is jobs.
.TP
.B \-\-percentage\-format value
Printf format of the charge. The default is %s%%.
.TP
.B \-\-icons value
Ascii or nerd. The default is ascii.
.TP
.B \-\-graph\-width value
Cells of the charge bar. The default is 10.
.TP
.B \-\-graph\-full value
A filled cell of the bar. The default is █.
.TP
.B \-\-graph\-empty value
An empty cell of the bar. The default is ░.
.TP
.B \-\-remain\-format value
