.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B BATTERY_REVAMPED_<SETTING>
The same as the option of that name, such as BATTERY_REVAMPED_INTERVAL for \-\-interval.
.TP
.B BATTERY_REVAMPED_THEME
The look, when \-\-theme is not given.
.TP
.B BATTERY_REVAMPED_ACCENT
A colour such as #CBA6F7 for the accent.
.TP
.B KODOUGU_THEME
The family look, when neither is given.
.TP
.B KODOUGU_ACCENT
The family accent, when the tool's is unset.
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
Turn colour off.
.SH TMUX OPTIONS
Every option above is read as the tmux option @battery_revamped_ followed by its name with underscores, such as @battery_revamped_popup_key, and the theme of every tmux\-revamped tool as @revamped_theme. The stored reading lives in @battery_revamped_percent, _status, _remain, _watts, _cycles, _health, _drain_rate and _history, with the time of each reading in options that end in _ts. apply records the placeholders the status line uses in @battery_revamped_published, the daemon writes each one to @battery_revamped_out_name and keeps its process id in @battery_revamped_ticker_pid.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 on any failure.
